  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isocarboxazid may be associated with Major Depressive Disorder through a pathway involving endogenous depression. This is supported by the shared indication of Endogenous Depression in all three paths, which in turn links to Vortioxetine and Tranylcypromine, both of which are indicated to treat Major Depressive Disorder. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Isocarboxazid and the condition, likely through a mechanism involving the modulation of depressive symptoms. The overlapping indications suggest that Isocarboxazid may act as a potential therapeutic agent for Major Depressive Disorder, possibly by influencing the endogenous depression pathway. The integration of these paths highlights the role of endogenous depression as a central node in the relationship between Isocarboxazid and the disorder, reinforcing the possibility of repurposing Isocarboxazid for this indication.",
